# UX-SPEC §3.8.7 — Help runs what it finds: a power user in a terminal presses `ctrl-s ?`, types
# "zoom" and `⏎`, and the terminal zooms, exactly as `ctrl-s z` would have done.
#
# The cursor starts on the best action that works where Help was opened, even though the
# Terminals guide is listed above it, and the action reaches the Workspace behind Help only
# after Help has handed the keyboard back. Zoom hides the tab strip, so its targets are the
# observable.
fixture: one-repo
await idle
key o
await screen == Workspace 20000
await targets["tabs.tab[0]"] exists 20000

key ctrl-s ?
await overlay == Dialog 10000
assert dialog.name == Help
await targets["help.here[0]"] exists 10000
shot help-in-terminal
type zoom
await dialog.fields[0].value == zoom 5000
await targets["help.run"] exists 5000
shot help-zoom
key enter
await overlay absent 10000
await targets["tabs.tab[0]"] absent 10000
assert screen == Workspace && mode == Terminal
shot zoomed

# `ctrl-s z` is the same toggle, so the key undoes what the row did.
key ctrl-s z
await targets["tabs.tab[0]"] exists 10000
quit
